description:
The tool to interact with the Network Orchestrator, the system that controls the BT network operations. 

It allows for:

- GET /locations/{name} : a set of network locations based on a customer {name}
- GET /definitions : gets the definitions of the available networking services
- GET /deployed/{name}: gets the currently deployed networking services based on a customer {name}
- DELETE /service : Deletes an existing networking service for a customer
- POST /service : Creates an existing networking service for a customer
- GET /metrics: Gets the metrics for a deployed connectivity service based on {name} and period in minutes {minutes}
- DELETE /test : Deletes an existing connectivity test for a customer
- POST /test : Creates an new connectivity test for a customer
- GET /apps/{name} : the IT applications based on a customer {name}


The networking orchestrator itself uses Kubernetes CRDs to control the networking operations state. Hence the responses from this Tool will be in a kubernetes CRD format.

